#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1f60e01-bcaa-538a-85d1-4c41aee48064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+6)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493335} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8870fe-f483-4a24-aa31-063adbde72e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\left(4x+6\\right)^4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f60e01-bcaa-538a-85d1-4c41aee48064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+6)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493335} :answer-field/id #uuid "74945d2f-3779-5856-8f0b-b1fe26940f82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c698fb8-2f47-52aa-ab20-d02b17699d11" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(4x+6)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=4x+6$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(4x+6{)}^{′}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+6{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6b327a-95b5-56cb-b8b1-80852501eb0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e6b327a-95b5-56cb-b8b1-80852501eb0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493327} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a534b2c-8471-58d8-901e-8ca326167938" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "97e8ab80-425a-5ce3-aeca-1b6c32080f6d" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-3},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=5x-3$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(5x-3)^{′}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5e2ea6-5eec-545e-bf02-640b9eb005aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df5e2ea6-5eec-545e-bf02-640b9eb005aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493334} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9beb5af-bf72-501b-8c38-28d625a4d182" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a645231c-c79c-561b-9b41-b96c53332e19" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-7{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})^{′}=5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6c1d0d-4c00-5981-9219-0c8e265c4f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d7603626fb60eb9cae8ed8155a1eb81d2a66a3c239468c93ccf7c0f0530a5193.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497747} {:answer/id #uuid "468e40cd-9cf9-5a6b-96e2-0dee3bac3ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/ac2fb8cd0a1e808bc599067860a3bf1af50a167e4ae71c8ad4d8a9329ebe6cb0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497750} {:answer/id #uuid "6f98bc0a-745d-5fe8-9adb-75bc94c5e580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/53c3f8c77c96b0925ce788a07b102555a1fca916d8ea20fd47fe6894c2eb46b5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497754} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0741d7-a6b1-5299-943c-c9df2fd77321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b2bb0b6f019af476eae3e76adb7ac2ef4745a6c4bdeae24cd4a40320b23f882b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497757} {:answer/id #uuid "fa366fab-7ce5-5d4f-8d88-5e08fc12f31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5f/5fcdd5b3c95340859bbb6f30dd3e80aa7396762e91187541bf68f64e2b21c1b3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e6c1d0d-4c00-5981-9219-0c8e265c4f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d7/d7603626fb60eb9cae8ed8155a1eb81d2a66a3c239468c93ccf7c0f0530a5193.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497747} :answer-field/id #uuid "714f5f25-99f5-58fb-9ddf-b6fc9c8a48c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b239726-9ec0-5ecb-8b93-7c8edf0b2f3f" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=-4x?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x \\\\  & =-4(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x \\\\  & =-4(1) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-4).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-4x.$ \n\n![](images/8b/8b008b94eebbd24ae51670447848ce2d644c067d43dd92d72de85b048358cc54.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497762 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "197e6448-d4b8-50c4-8753-532544dcd499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/99/992d82dfeac6b0a73453363ca57efaa9fe70b2b5ccd7cd1712b5772f09c224d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497744} {:answer/id #uuid "42221fb0-f700-5e55-a7e6-33f0cb67bcb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a82731b726d091769fdf10ca7f5d7ee87816cd490f933aaf1fc2c19c0701603.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497749} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac7786b-a678-552f-b339-f52f193863ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8ef5652a5d1a90b6874dc19a87b7109fc2144507a587fb1daab19c0c3442d4df.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497751} {:answer/id #uuid "ad159fd3-feff-5d67-88af-d4e81768184a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b3/b3be73566253173f2ca88649fd585cced2cab7cddc27be7c40eeae9d8db2cc09.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497759} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f0b6a4-03c2-5777-8ad1-670384f66a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d517f4c1af2fbd48ec41131ce7dec1aeb4d2c50514e53360ab043a4daa93552.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "197e6448-d4b8-50c4-8753-532544dcd499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/99/992d82dfeac6b0a73453363ca57efaa9fe70b2b5ccd7cd1712b5772f09c224d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497744} :answer-field/id #uuid "24d238d3-c42b-5a24-b6da-36a8047d399e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9992e41-e63d-5336-a605-48b1d684791a" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=-3x?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\  & =-3(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\  & =-3(1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-3).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-3x.$ \n\n![](images/08/08e854b04d47ff670b197a2a0c7b51c13eb135626e0ed6cdfd24368d4032f259.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497764 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc17c22-f348-5c67-921e-bb49f7e4bc08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/afb86fd4a7ffd591dfbbc6e8ee837b33b943972212b04b15f9040b310b0abdba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497746} {:answer/id #uuid "5656dea6-87b8-5765-a05d-162629ac3306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39ae505504b452e87f70c4b555914b597ff0d3859f54f1f4d2ed5516c73131da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497752} {:answer/id #uuid "59705c30-8f9f-56b2-8c1d-4816e1357d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c4d21e0fdbdb082c1efdd50936da2cd8c131be9b5ac3fa0fa85a73f8c11cf48.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497753} {:answer/id #uuid "a43ac8a2-cf32-55c4-b2d4-693e23dc22b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d1/d17e0a44ef03d6110f031a8ab6f0bf63b478a263754bbab63124e880546aef28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497758} {:answer/id #uuid "cd48e67e-3c17-53e8-a38a-e16bd3b4647f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c7577f7033f36315d50748424d7a8db635e9aecd4c88c9ed4626f3294bc6c2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59705c30-8f9f-56b2-8c1d-4816e1357d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c4d21e0fdbdb082c1efdd50936da2cd8c131be9b5ac3fa0fa85a73f8c11cf48.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497753} :answer-field/id #uuid "77551351-5d0a-512a-acd9-8abceb71136c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffd546da-09fc-5649-b60d-749bd09256a6" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=-1x?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1x \\\\  & =-1(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-1x \\\\  & =-1(1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-1x.$ \n\n![](images/73/7322801cf231391f58d39f2fad42b779e04fc1b81b686bcb3291ebfee5651226.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06fa8c2f-5b1f-5063-8e88-0b913061880c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30ea4f86a1a588cd617779bc001935f50b7fa358ecca86efeaf26bde27642627.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497766} {:answer/id #uuid "09af78ca-b5c2-58ed-aee4-4ddfc7a7f013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3b91b84281ef5b4936438c7e92935cbaf15d17ee50b33a27a7bed638391ef74.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497767} {:answer/id #uuid "29968d51-b8a6-5bee-82fc-d738be24cc8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b9758c660c06a62ba10ca7ced102655a3a8f376d31d9c4ef73ec9ea8b33e769b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497770} {:answer/id #uuid "7083980a-a87f-5d35-b45a-36f6cd7e349b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/07b33747d01621cb73ae464999a8d6a135f0dc579f9e50b250f34b3df9ca4783.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497779} {:answer/id #uuid "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497786} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad570f02-ebbc-528a-ba9a-40d1735ee18e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a903cf9-42ce-5563-9b36-303a8f1c1320" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x-3.$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x-3.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-(0)-3=-3,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)-3=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-(2)-3=-5,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)-3=-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $-6$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c9/c96b7da7b073986de68a557df8a9dbde16d39566c87eb0b5ba6ac62bd40da7c4.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x-3.$\n\n![](images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "505696e7-5c70-5bfb-9d5d-53a811375cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e65396cb057b7306ae81557f25d24f797e736ad37c09ddb0e67ee19c4e9ab318.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497773} {:answer/id #uuid "685c2324-6319-5bc5-b432-4f7efc03eacb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/db/dbddb21434456cdcb99c4ba0660c65615c97538ccbdcf2d6057e855d0d30f8f9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497778} {:answer/id #uuid "816e9948-7eb3-5b5d-9fb6-b4ad3fb7ff4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4bb98a9deb3f1049e3b2eeffca7deccfefb79fd5d893b89940be52fbce397d8a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497780} {:answer/id #uuid "8497b882-b57f-5efb-b03e-5229284a8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497781} {:answer/id #uuid "e100f2db-5cdc-57b9-ba80-cfeb83c61519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54c37e2aadc0f1a3db8ec1f39905b1e694804df7680999079f1d2a2017c09794.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8497b882-b57f-5efb-b03e-5229284a8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497781} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f305ae-b441-5bc6-833a-ae8108df72ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5da1545d-7bf4-538f-94f3-464d21187a82" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x-6.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)-6=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)-6=-2,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)-6=0.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/95/958c5a848a09e43832324b8afb000348c7630cd2c42e99a51215d48d9895a00e.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of  $y=2x-6.$\n\n![](images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b68311-0695-52e7-984f-b1f413574531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f59cdf977a5aa60bea4bbe522a20e29c3d13caa13ce178b5038569da0282bf04.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497768} {:answer/id #uuid "10291a72-b265-5a7e-ae36-03727e2c077a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d8/d89b7a9495d61d6c67332c05aa99d35957782b600b447bb0a70dbf3595857f83.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497769} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb40a26-7dd0-53a3-8f8b-50d6ae6b03aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497772} {:answer/id #uuid "c411d8f7-79b2-5537-91be-c623daad8c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/15bdb2e49885cb6bc9ea7aeccff0cb3227504f5b122f0f16e51bc2e6154d01c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497783} {:answer/id #uuid "dcebd751-9faf-5113-a03b-26d02cbb100e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c62998935843f79fcf2007edbfe243071b75c9ceb63babf46cad3c6aa507291c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cb40a26-7dd0-53a3-8f8b-50d6ae6b03aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497772} :answer-field/id #uuid "645e1d5a-90c9-50c4-b1ae-f7aff3a3dba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67365bc6-453f-5a19-82a4-9817c6e05a99" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-6.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=(1)-6=-5,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-6=-4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-6=-3.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/99/99188f2a0f8de0054a6375a88a11242bea7e4799cc17552cd9ba0dd00d5a0788.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n![](images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498490 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb8d995d-0d7c-54d6-8c3f-aa2cc0e562a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498216} {:answer/id #uuid "ce93c3a1-776f-5631-aafd-89bd7f33c5b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498268} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe50e10-ec80-526e-8c44-4ebed28fb715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498270} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f112d4-518e-59d2-a8ae-9b7896ed80c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498304} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e01110-89b2-522a-b30e-7b877b8b16ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfe50e10-ec80-526e-8c44-4ebed28fb715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498270} :answer-field/id #uuid "30362ef7-7428-53da-a7f2-7fe7cc3d3d5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09c35a82-4469-5857-aed4-331c374b8ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126895" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0db447407835f74476edd20ed5327ff3cc570905f744bbc6c29a66926913ecb5.png)\n\nCalculate $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}(1-4y)\\,dx+(2+5x)\\,dy,\n$$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=1-4y$ and $Q(x,y)=2+5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-(-4))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 5\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a658638-403e-5ab9-a8f1-33237b22ab86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497887} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5743a8-8fd6-5394-b293-eb9fd93fef49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497979} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9eb833-f8ff-5a68-9ca4-2b64e1730afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498127} {:answer/id #uuid "9d75ef58-226e-55fd-b151-11b12d2230bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498153} {:answer/id #uuid "f496543e-10b7-5658-8197-b5afed861eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a658638-403e-5ab9-a8f1-33237b22ab86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497887} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7d01b58-0857-54fb-bdf6-61d33e711eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2260d96-b984-5295-801c-28a9593008a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126851" :question/problem "![](images/e9/e9892ef4efa3481ad02f7b8e38f1bae1876b196627204521d011656010297281.png)\n\nSuppose that $F$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ defined over the region $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=16,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=6,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=4,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ is oriented counterclockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of $$\n\\displaystyle {∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/b2/b20b2b911c2a417c26fa951d9b28efa296c265df25e9d06b635ef4846267b93b.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =16+6+4 \\\\  & =26.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498676} {:answer/id #uuid "643d71ec-95bc-5042-8b51-322a436c9046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498683} {:answer/id #uuid "80feb855-589a-53c3-bac3-61637b4af9e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498690} {:answer/id #uuid "e967faa4-e8a6-581c-a3cf-38284b6b90c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498712} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf14a96-818d-5db6-9c66-a0d3175bb6b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498676} :answer-field/id #uuid "fffeded8-fcf5-542f-a921-ded34513e23b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f863f32-c463-5f07-9482-1c6f6e74c019" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c714262b9da22ea9ad859817db86a3aaf0b29ef811246aedc969bc9999c0348.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0)$, $B(-1,4)$ and $C(3,6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (0) & =1(-3)+3 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (4) & =1(-1)+3 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,6)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (6) & =1(3)+3 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b01faa9-1661-5d2c-8b15-89c1d529166b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498665} {:answer/id #uuid "2773d5bd-6a1e-5e0f-bdc4-1f27d274f0fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498671} {:answer/id #uuid "4546836a-abb8-583d-8041-3599332cf4de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498678} {:answer/id #uuid "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498693} {:answer/id #uuid "961c8a45-200e-5ff7-841b-40c1e1f1d099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498693} :answer-field/id #uuid "02799bef-6cfd-5d9e-bca3-3026a3cc6d51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "12a60b9c-85ce-50af-b45d-06caed36a198" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cee718f18c9ef081b3e90a70d4db00ef0339d7d5f0b87423f7c5687709471a6.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-5x-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,9),B(-1,4)$ and $C(1,-7).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,9)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (9) & =-5(-2)-2 \\\\ 9 & =8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (4) & =-5(-1)-2 \\\\ 4 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (-7) & =-5(1)-2 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a90128e-f77f-5ec3-9038-8600c7b3dcfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498681} {:answer/id #uuid "627354bc-e225-5d3c-9eda-85b7e4603569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498682} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0560a4-412e-54e3-91ff-603a3b02dcd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498688} {:answer/id #uuid "8098dcbf-4d2e-5f36-b4e9-f6ca59744fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498689} {:answer/id #uuid "a27987d5-3a9e-5baf-b1a3-d4be781d9d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a90128e-f77f-5ec3-9038-8600c7b3dcfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498681} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed72d909-9af6-5dcf-9647-d3ab941b4b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21a9c497-cf26-5338-8f2e-52de8c6489fc" :question/problem "![](images/70/70b04ef6ee89c2bf06db99444f1f89afbe2ea15871f8f79da29668f7be3f9f97.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,-2)$, $B(1,4)$ and $C(2,4).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (-2) & =2(-1)+0 \\\\ -2 & =-2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(1)+0 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,4)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(2)+0 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2517ee62-3508-5043-99a6-8cbff4a054bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498670} {:answer/id #uuid "49484dad-6a3e-55b6-a9bc-7f95d103cd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498679} {:answer/id #uuid "6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498686} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6fe6ee-5189-5bb5-9dc1-3ca7c751bd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498696} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1b1055-64cd-5ad9-a4f4-4ba68a08c842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498686} :answer-field/id #uuid "030b1280-3f72-5e40-9687-4451485960c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "277a1bc9-d733-576e-9af4-fb70571bb178" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb6b3f51e0e61f72015505469f9fd6e6aa2d5e5b550825e4c761fc78f535ef59.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-7)$, $B(-1,1)$ and $C(1,5).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (-7) & =3(-3)+2 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (1) & =3(-1)+2 \\\\ 1 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,5)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+2 \\\\ 5 & =5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b24e4af-347a-5ac2-9514-dd6e178db687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498668} {:answer/id #uuid "70b48381-828b-5d40-b1db-1850c4bb5fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498687} {:answer/id #uuid "aef1cd6c-325f-57b3-b55a-22367510cec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498702} {:answer/id #uuid "b7497970-afdd-59b5-8946-7e774cc44e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498705} {:answer/id #uuid "e81db796-7d07-5404-a2e6-282ce3e715b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aef1cd6c-325f-57b3-b55a-22367510cec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498702} :answer-field/id #uuid "c99296eb-61a0-59b5-b855-4521c40f6736" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a390081c-820e-5ce3-b17e-0ab4001a9339" :question/problem "![](images/18/18df2c651366aa361dd4210585c0f9d0607af2f93b6c8b29b14ad1144907fb94.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x-4?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0),B(-2,-2)$ and $C(2,-8).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (0) & =-2(-3)-4 \\\\ 0 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (-2) & =-2(-2)-4 \\\\ -2 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (-8) & =-2(2)-4 \\\\ -8 & =-8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d413d8c-3f61-5d64-83db-8f504335c5bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498673} {:answer/id #uuid "3c85b355-307a-57db-947f-d3ef8d268d84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498677} {:answer/id #uuid "83323bd5-5d34-562b-8783-b053fe0eef22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498691} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f856d5-e5e8-54b8-ab43-051a8533362c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498700} {:answer/id #uuid "da7c1cda-1a6a-51a1-bee2-23c37eac0b62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8f856d5-e5e8-54b8-ab43-051a8533362c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498700} :answer-field/id #uuid "50fbda0d-f2a0-59f8-8288-e3b71a72d78f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac37c3c8-b208-5c81-a00d-e1bd9d503cf5" :question/problem "![](images/21/210db4ba3df7f9004c6ffe53336ce3e42d4156841560813478c404353b204c0c.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-4x+1?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,3),B(1,-1)$ and $C(2,-7).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (3) & =-4(0)+1 \\\\ 3 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-1) & =-4(1)+1 \\\\ -1 & =-3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-7) & =-4(2)+1 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498663} {:answer/id #uuid "0a037906-7560-5a7f-af3a-df39ea31c7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498664} {:answer/id #uuid "2e04fce8-d81f-5c10-9a2d-ce00e7cc6157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498674} {:answer/id #uuid "64c6d466-8db0-5469-a154-b446a630e557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498685} {:answer/id #uuid "cb659afb-f587-5d6a-8397-672e2e9f924f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498663} :answer-field/id #uuid "9124fd28-3c96-58aa-a8b1-46f977a63903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0bb51db-df3a-5c24-9053-c8f5081141e9" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1aa0849898f763eedd84d050a7bd7c24bbb10c8f89c81e3f533622252330814e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+4.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-5)$, $B(1,5)$ and $C(2,10).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (-5) & =3(-3)+4 \\\\ -5 & =-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+4 \\\\ 5 & =7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,10)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (10) & =3(2)+4 \\\\ 10 & =10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32181eed-9458-5ccf-acc4-92033b733168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498675} {:answer/id #uuid "6485fbd6-7602-59e9-b7db-664adfdbcd5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498684} {:answer/id #uuid "a768ab80-55c6-5d51-80fc-ee9ca1c3c7c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498699} {:answer/id #uuid "b31cf4f4-e928-5d0a-810e-cf15a16aed3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498704} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9fccde-11ea-51fa-a5a6-450785e2da15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a768ab80-55c6-5d51-80fc-ee9ca1c3c7c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498699} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d72100-1cce-5a74-8205-dd9bc89e56ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbacf92b-66e8-58cd-bc32-e7d565177fbf" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1ff37e7ea63a62de2a1ccbf59c53225b739be305f9e87f7aceca7735ba210bbd.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-3x?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,8),B(0,-2)$ and $C(2,-6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (8) & =-3(-2)+0 \\\\ 8 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (-2) & =-3(0)+0 \\\\ -2 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (-6) & =-3(2)+0 \\\\ -6 & =-6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501323 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3da477-2f8c-5b2b-8534-55a21ba63377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501316} {:answer/id #uuid "25f25fe2-2d7e-54ee-967f-6bb9248a110b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501319} {:answer/id #uuid "277c7b29-7430-521f-9d76-62c8fd5674b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501320} {:answer/id #uuid "92cee00b-fc75-54a9-b753-d48fe2943e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501325} {:answer/id #uuid "bae18ee6-b3b9-5327-ad96-6d55d7e27bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c3da477-2f8c-5b2b-8534-55a21ba63377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501316} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1108d84-a4e2-5397-a2f7-9adbc9f6a9b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "61c31858-4aad-578b-a21e-e968c5ca8b40" :question/problem "![](images/76/7688f7536a66b7a737d58031b9b8752aabaa84a914ff5deb799e7060d7a90aeb.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=-4x+\\frac{2}{3}$\n\nII. $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(6,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/cb/cbec3e69d5f8a5bbcfc7d97d95c9f3d3ec93be63b1c8de2ceba3e3a24a9dba13.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-4x+\\frac{2}{3}.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =-4(0)+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-4x+\\frac{2}{3}$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(6,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =-\\frac{2}{3}(0)+4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}(6)+4 \\\\ 0 & =-4+4 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(6,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =\\frac{2}{3}(0)+4 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =\\frac{2}{3}(6)+4 \\\\ 0 & =4+4 \\\\ 0 & =8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+4$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that represented the line in the graph was $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x+4,$ corresponding to answer choice II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015abcb0-80a5-5dc1-b79f-79d7198d8b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501315} {:answer/id #uuid "1d75fe37-e4ce-5bc4-98f8-d2fb16b56012" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501318} {:answer/id #uuid "7d397adc-2e01-5cd8-a945-f4855a2fd4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501324} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3194ba-e75e-59ea-b78e-7f3fe9b442f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501327} {:answer/id #uuid "e6c58012-7269-5610-aef9-dbc7d838d8f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6c58012-7269-5610-aef9-dbc7d838d8f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501333} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a010cc-cba0-5af2-91cb-dae10509e3db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b3d6f732-ed9f-51fe-87bd-f9f387742c79" :question/problem "![](images/87/87cbbd5a53079bb2cd744e1af18e901f6e54239a0fc6330984659c75cbdd3509.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y+3x=9$\n\nII. $\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3$\n\nIII. $y=-3x+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,9)$ and $(3,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/c3/c3a0113d32377bd9bac1569081dce1caad04e1cd385805fbb225c3964e7f85d7.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y+3x=9.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9)+3(0) & =9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓ \\\\ (0)+3(3) & =9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+3x=9$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}(9)+(0) & =3 \\\\ 3+0 & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}(0)+(3) & =3 \\\\ 0+3 & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=-3x+9.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9) & =-3(0)+9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-3(3)+9 \\\\ 0 & =-9+9 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3x+9$ is  an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nAll the given equations represented the line in the graph. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116550ec-7c28-5e18-9fdd-f2d1f181ab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501317} {:answer/id #uuid "4566a58e-dd27-57f2-8c17-67e13d84f401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501321} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9607e4-f2bb-5686-8bd2-b386551546bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501326} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e72227-20c4-5321-a16a-1705dfdcf169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501328} {:answer/id #uuid "cf447eac-1836-54a3-8082-5758760bcbed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf447eac-1836-54a3-8082-5758760bcbed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501331} :answer-field/id #uuid "5912bad9-fd12-5d7e-8bfc-20dae374c49f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ff7154d8-1178-59c1-89cf-d6727039f41b" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f0218ba02ef7305b1f22582379d15e8da24c859a239b45130c053aa5c3f8cde1.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=-3x+\\frac{3}{8}$\n\nII. $y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{3}{8}x+3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,3)$ and $(8,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/f1/f193f5ea70aa459427c5c4abecfdb74c3e12c6de4e22522d71f5ca1f6b1b9cc1.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-3x+\\frac{3}{8}.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3) & =-3(0)+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3x+\\frac{3}{8}$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,3)$ and $B(8,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3) & =-\\frac{3}{8}(0)+3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-\\frac{3}{8}(8)+3 \\\\ 0 & =-3+3 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{3}{8}x+3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,3)$ and $B(8,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3) & =\\frac{3}{8}(0)+3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =\\frac{3}{8}(8)+3 \\\\ 0 & =3+3 \\\\ 0 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{3}{8}x+3$ is *not* equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that represented the line in the graph was $y=-\\frac{3}{8}x+3,$ corresponding to answer choice II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "379ce176-b85b-5473-ac5c-c334e33ade53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502889} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa0d404-d0fc-5e09-8e4b-7fcc8eed12b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}x^{-13/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502896} {:answer/id #uuid "4028963f-e622-507c-92ba-3fe653d44e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{7}x^{-20/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502898} {:answer/id #uuid "48e20e30-98ef-545f-8564-315ec67ca5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502906} {:answer/id #uuid "d873e68a-b191-51b0-8a82-9ae3df09c4fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{7}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48e20e30-98ef-545f-8564-315ec67ca5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502906} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d70d54-a73e-59c2-9e26-72bd20515cfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "054c92af-f6c0-5cb6-8c52-c81bf5740a21" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{13}}}$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Note that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{13}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{13/7}}={x}^{-13/7}.\n$$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{13}{7}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{13}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-13/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-13/7+1}}{-\\frac{13}{7}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{-6/7}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{6{x}^{6/7}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e03f87-24cd-5a1f-85f6-21fa74293d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{9}x^{-16/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502861} {:answer/id #uuid "04c21815-61ed-534e-ad04-3d35a62aa2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502862} {:answer/id #uuid "24baf7d8-b08d-52e8-aacf-0f682f6c25f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{9}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502877} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a05915-00e3-5287-9df3-ec5051320330" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}x^{-7/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502937} {:answer/id #uuid "d1cf8368-4008-5f0c-b393-98dc8c2b3340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04c21815-61ed-534e-ad04-3d35a62aa2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502862} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d96cda-06e3-5949-b59a-136c6439133a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ea9e5d9-602f-5599-818f-aa6b87eda7f7" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-7/9}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{7}{9}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-7/9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-7/9+1}}{(-\\frac{7}{9}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2/9}}{\\left(\\frac{2}{9}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2/9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3db7372d-b7c0-5c4e-be87-53e9e865f128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-8/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502895} {:answer/id #uuid "4341f9bb-aabc-509a-b456-9aef502ddeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}x^{-2/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502904} {:answer/id #uuid "515bed00-c253-59e6-90ff-ea177c4df26c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-2/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502908} {:answer/id #uuid "6542b0ac-8e88-518e-93f4-c4f361379998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x^{-5/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502912} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d66349-73d9-5894-8ea5-62c18d22ca86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x^{-2/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1d66349-73d9-5894-8ea5-62c18d22ca86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}x^{-2/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502952} :answer-field/id #uuid "8878aff2-5da1-5cae-8ac0-c802b9fa22f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "24409f16-92eb-5e3a-9a94-2612754d8d1a" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{5}}}$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Note that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{5}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/3}}={x}^{-5/3}.\n$$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-5/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/3+1}}{-\\frac{5}{3}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-2/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2/3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ca6ae77-d4eb-5628-bf2d-2ad81668a6fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}x^{3/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502893} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8ee872-c2aa-5ac4-be85-d82e9c4ef936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}x^{-11/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502907} {:answer/id #uuid "727e1873-0bcc-5e7f-8015-b4f278888e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}x^{-4/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502919} {:answer/id #uuid "c398c1d7-925b-5ee5-a8fa-61cab36aa511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{3}x^{3/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502946} {:answer/id #uuid "fa18ec9f-eb7c-5a17-b374-3ab9b1f1d7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}x^{3/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa18ec9f-eb7c-5a17-b374-3ab9b1f1d7cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}x^{3/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502961} :answer-field/id #uuid "42e84933-a55b-529f-9a48-2720e2d4ea8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502903}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2838d5a7-98fc-5b74-838a-12c9f0c1d487" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-4/7}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{4}{7}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-4/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4/7+1}}{(-\\frac{4}{7}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/7}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{7}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}{x}^{3/7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27715ac4-7080-5ffe-be40-e664b63285a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}x^{-7/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502878} {:answer/id #uuid "3193dee8-6d38-5f64-9116-9e39da2d7bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{7}x^{-7/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502882} {:answer/id #uuid "421826bb-b2d5-5fb8-947d-ac92615073de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}x^{-13/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502901} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b35749-3d6f-5507-92fc-8f661d4354b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}x^{-7/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502936} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fcac92-9f4c-5be7-a469-98066cd54d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{7}x^{-10/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3193dee8-6d38-5f64-9116-9e39da2d7bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{7}x^{-7/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502882} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ddf54d7-8f99-5eb4-8c0a-845692b3564f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35340db4-7b99-5255-81e2-d140281bf3c1" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{10}}}$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Note that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{10}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{10/3}}={x}^{-10/3}.\n$$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{10}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{10}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-10/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-10/3+1}}{-\\frac{10}{3}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{7}{x}^{-7/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{7{x}^{7/3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12095852-ce4c-5c59-b9b1-192364d03345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}x^{-1/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502866} {:answer/id #uuid "80af63e6-f7fb-5178-9c4a-d96bedf2c287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x^{-5/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502922} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d97a02-3bcb-5f85-9497-a9db944bdb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502942} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d65c81-82ee-5c39-9813-d7adc6117dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502955} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b9e661-3c29-5b89-b031-ae16b8d1203b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b9e661-3c29-5b89-b031-ae16b8d1203b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502957} :answer-field/id #uuid "10312bb4-8cd0-5e43-95e8-b8afad9283e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a5e9787-8ef9-5e19-99e9-70e48a27adcf" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-1/4}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-1/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/4+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/4}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d738aac-dbe8-544c-8e1d-2595eca3d13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{-1/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502880} {:answer/id #uuid "6a447127-79f8-57b4-9456-cc1dc920e3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x^{-5/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502913} {:answer/id #uuid "907f822e-c090-559b-9aba-2e8311fdac55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}x^{-9/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502929} {:answer/id #uuid "a06d15c6-bae0-59f6-910b-7f074de70fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}x^{-1/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502935} {:answer/id #uuid "c035fb66-b8a0-5b74-85ee-dba3437624aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x^{-1/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c035fb66-b8a0-5b74-85ee-dba3437624aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x^{-1/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502945} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc2d6790-5efe-5373-be98-3094e21928cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40665566-8355-550d-acf0-8fd3e706266d" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/4}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/4}}={x}^{-5/4}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{5}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-5/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/4+1}}{(-\\frac{5}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/4}}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-4{x}^{-1/4}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{{x}^{1/4}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0079a791-7df9-5dd7-bdf0-9fde624e2bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}x^{5/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502860} {:answer/id #uuid "337d5a89-e1d3-5a29-83bb-5d3c21780cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}x^{-2/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502884} {:answer/id #uuid "369f6c33-6557-5d15-9e0e-5f461bceaa53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}x^{-9/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502888} {:answer/id #uuid "384fd8fa-5c2e-5502-b800-d8f574d73937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}x^{5/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502890} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d5023d-868a-5e5b-8467-7a19e219606f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}x^{5/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2d5023d-868a-5e5b-8467-7a19e219606f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}x^{5/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502939} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b3ca9a2-ba9f-55a3-b9c0-c0e7936f7ddc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ac48824-980d-5dff-8c73-e9a877cd9d8e" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-2/7}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{2}{7}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-2/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-2/7+1}}{(-\\frac{2}{7}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/7}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{7}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}{x}^{5/7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
